window.LINES={"hello": "Hello, scientist! Welcome to Body Town. It's Grand Opening Day, and I'm the mayor!", "snooze_in": "Meet Snooze, our town inspector. He's a sausage dog. A very long one.", "snooze_asleep": "Oh dear. He's asleep. Again.", "miccheck": "Let's check I can hear you. Say: Wake up, Snooze!", "heardyou": "I heard you! So did Snooze. Look, he's awake!", "nohear": "I can't hear you right now. That's okay. You can tap instead.", "tapmode": "Today you can tap your answers. Tap Snooze to wake him up!", "help": "Can you be my Chief Engineer today? Body Town needs fixing.", "problem": "Snooze napped on the job. He knocked every signpost into a muddle!", "dig": "Snooze is digging! He's found an old map from Ancient Egypt. Look, the heart!", "egypt_air": "Egyptian doctors thought the heart and its tubes carried air.", "egypt_why": "Why did they think that? Pick the best clue.", "egypt_ans": "Yes! In dead bodies, the blood had drained out. So the tubes held air.", "today": "Today we know they carry blood. Scanners and operations show it, in living people.", "ladder_intro": "How do cells, tissues and organs work together? Body Town is built like a ladder.", "ladder_trick": "Remember our trick? Can Tiny Owls Sing Opera?", "ladder_order": "Put the steps in order. Start with the smallest.", "ladder_wrong": "Not that step yet. Which one is smaller?", "lad_cell": "Cell. The tiny building block.", "lad_tissue": "Tissue. A group of the same type of cells.", "lad_organ": "Organ. Different tissues, working together.", "lad_system": "Organ system. A group of organs, working together.", "lad_organism": "Organism. A whole living thing. That's you!", "sys_q": "So, what is an organ system?", "sys_ans": "A group of organs that work together, to do an important job.", "heart_tissues": "Your heart is one organ. Tap the three tissues it is made of.", "paper_tissue": "Ha! Not that kind of tissue. That one's for sneezes!", "heart_ans": "Muscle, fat and nerve tissue. Three tissues, one organ!", "stomach_cells": "Muscle cells make muscle tissue. Nerve cells make nerve tissue.", "stomach_organ": "Put both tissues together, and you get the stomach. An organ!", "stomach_q": "Which organ system is the stomach part of?", "stomach_ans": "The digestive system! It breaks down food.", "watch": "Remember this bit from the video? Let's watch.", "buildintro": "Engineers need the right words. Let's build the team names.", "tapbeats": "Tap the beats in the right order.", "w_digestive": "This system breaks down food. It has three beats.", "w_circulatory": "This system carries blood round your body. It has five beats.", "w_urinary": "This system gets rid of waste. It has four beats.", "w_locomotor": "This system moves you from place to place. It has four beats.", "notyet": "Not that one yet. Which beat comes next?", "built": "You built it!", "drum": "Now tap the drum once for each beat, and say the beats with me.", "sayword": "Now say the whole word.", "again": "Let's try once more, slowly. Listen.", "yousay": "Now you say it.", "goodtry": "Good try! We'll practise that one again another day.", "n_digestive": "Digestive.", "n_circulatory": "Circulatory.", "n_urinary": "Urinary.", "n_locomotor": "Locomotor.", "s_di": "Di.", "s_ges": "Ges.", "s_tive": "Tive.", "s_cir": "Cir.", "s_cu": "Cu.", "s_la": "La.", "s_to": "To.", "s_ry": "Ry.", "s_u": "U.", "s_ri": "Ri.", "s_nar": "Nar.", "s_y": "Y.", "s_lo": "Lo.", "s_co": "Co.", "s_mo": "Mo.", "s_tor": "Tor.", "digest_means": "Digest means break down food. Sorry, Snooze, it's not a digestive biscuit!", "circ_means": "Circ means circle. Blood goes round and round, in a circle.", "urin_means": "Urine is liquid waste. Urinary means to do with urine.", "loco_means": "Loco means place. Motor means mover. Moving from place to place!", "wordsdone": "Four team names built! Now let's fix those signposts.", "sign_intro": "Every building must join the right team. Let's fix the signposts!", "sign_how": "Look at each organ. Which team is it in? Say the team, or tap its box.", "c_gullet": "The gullet carries food from your mouth to your stomach. Digestive!", "c_stomach": "The stomach breaks up food. Digestive!", "c_smallint": "The small intestine breaks up food and absorbs it. Digestive!", "c_largeint": "The large intestine takes water out of unwanted food. Digestive!", "c_rectum": "The rectum stores waste. Digestive!", "c_liver": "The liver makes and stores useful substances. It helps the digestive team.", "c_heart": "The heart pumps blood. Circulatory!", "c_vessels": "Blood vessels are tubes that carry blood. Circulatory!", "c_windpipe": "The windpipe, or trachea, takes air to your lungs. Breathing!", "c_lungs": "The lungs get oxygen into your blood. Breathing!", "c_diaphragm": "The diaphragm is a sheet of muscle. It helps you breathe. Breathing!", "c_kidneys": "The kidneys clean your blood and make urine. Urinary!", "c_bladder": "The bladder stores urine, until you go to the toilet. Urinary!", "c_brain": "The brain controls your body. Nervous!", "c_spinal": "The spinal cord runs down the middle of your back. Nervous!", "c_nerves": "Nerves carry messages everywhere, like wires. Nervous!", "c_muscles": "Muscles pull on your bones to move them. Locomotor!", "c_bones": "Bones hold you up. Locomotor! Sorry, Snooze, that bone isn't for you.", "sign_wrong": "Hmm. What does that organ do? Which team needs it?", "kidneys_40": "Fun fact! Your kidneys clean all of your blood every forty minutes.", "vessels_km": "A grown-up has over one hundred thousand kilometres of blood vessels.", "earth4": "Your book says that could go around the Earth four times!", "sign_done": "All the signposts are fixed! Body Town looks brilliant.", "map_intro": "Now let's learn all six teams by heart. Here's a trick.", "dogs_trick": "Can Dogs Usually Nap By Lakes?", "dogs_order": "Put the six teams in order. Use the trick to help you.", "dogs_wrong": "Not that one yet. Say the trick slowly.", "d_c": "C is for circulatory.", "d_d": "D is for digestive.", "d_u": "U is for urinary.", "d_n": "N is for nervous.", "d_b": "B is for breathing. Its other name is the respiratory system.", "d_l": "L is for locomotor.", "jobs_intro": "Each team runs one service. Listen to the job, then tap the system.", "j_digest": "Which system breaks down food, and takes nutrients into your blood?", "j_circ": "Which system carries oxygen and nutrients all around your body?", "j_breath": "Which system takes air in and out, and gets oxygen into your blood?", "j_urin": "Which system gets rid of waste that your body makes?", "j_nerv": "Which system lets you sense things, and carries messages very fast?", "j_loco": "Which system moves you from place to place?", "body_wrong": "Not that one. Think about the job, and try again.", "gren_intro": "Remember Mrs Gren? Each team helps with a life process.", "gren_q": "Which life process does this team help with?", "ga_digest": "Nutrition! Getting the substances you need from food.", "ga_urin": "Excretion! Getting rid of waste.", "ga_nerv": "Sensitivity! Sensing things around you, and reacting.", "ga_breath": "Respiration! Oxygen helps your cells release energy.", "ga_loco": "Movement! Changing position.", "oxy_q": "Tricky one! Air reaches your lungs. How does oxygen get to your toes?", "oxy_ans": "The breathing system only takes oxygen in. The circulatory system carries it everywhere.", "oxy_relay": "It's a relay race! The lungs pass oxygen to the blood. The blood delivers it.", "map_done": "Map complete! You know all six teams.", "breaktime": "You've worked hard, engineer. Time for a brain break!", "bb_intro": "Stand up! Let's give every team a workout.", "bb_pulse": "Two fingers on your wrist. Feel that little beat? Circulatory team!", "bb_breathe": "Hands on your chest. Breathe in slowly. And out. Breathing team!", "bb_kidney": "Hands on your back, just above your waist. Hello, kidneys! Urinary team!", "bb_trace": "Trace the food path, from your mouth down to your tummy. Digestive team!", "bb_nose": "Close your eyes. Touch your nose with one finger. Nervous team!", "bb_march": "March on the spot! Knees up high! Locomotor team!", "bb_nap": "And now… nap by the lake. Pretend to snore!", "bb_snooze": "Oh no! Snooze really fell asleep. Wake him up!", "bb_awake": "He's awake! Great moving. Your brain is ready again.", "garden_intro": "Body Town has a garden. Do plants have organ systems?", "garden_yes": "Yes, they do! A plant has a water transport system.", "garden_tap": "Tap the three organs in the water transport system.", "pl_root": "The roots take in water from the soil.", "pl_stem": "The stem carries the water up.", "pl_leaf": "The leaves lose water into the air.", "pl_flower": "A flower is an organ. But it's not in this team.", "water_how": "Why does water keep flowing up? Tap a leaf to find out.", "holes": "Leaves have tiny holes. Water evaporates out of them, into the air.", "pulled": "So more water is pulled up, all the way from the roots.", "xylem_q": "Which tissue carries water in all three organs?", "xylem_ans": "Xylem! It's in the roots, the stem and the leaves.", "root_ladder": "A root has its own ladder. Put it in order.", "root_done": "Root hair cells make root hair tissue. It helps make the root.", "leaf_test": "Snooze has a question. Does a leaf lose more water from its top, or underneath?", "test_how": "How could we find out? Pick the fair test.", "test_ans": "Cover the top of one leaf with jelly. Cover the underside of another. Weigh them each day.", "test_fair": "Keep everything else the same. Same plant, same size leaves, same place.", "test_result": "Most leaves have more tiny holes underneath. So the underside usually loses more.", "hosp_intro": "Welcome to Body Town Hospital. Sometimes an organ doesn't work properly.", "biopsy_what": "A doctor may take a tiny piece of tissue to look at. This is a biopsy.", "biopsy_beats": "Bi. Op. Sy. Bio means life. Opsy means looking.", "slide": "It goes on a slide. A coverslip keeps it flat, and stops it drying out.", "compare": "Here are two samples, X and Y. Look closely at the nuclei.", "cancer_q": "In some cancer cells, the nuclei become very large. Which sample might be cancer?", "cancer_ans": "Sample Y. Its nuclei are very large. This helps doctors find the problem, and plan a treatment.", "heart_sign_q": "How might a doctor notice that a heart isn't working well?", "heart_sign_ans": "A pulse that's too fast or too slow. Or getting out of breath very easily.", "fix_or_replace": "Sometimes an organ can't be made better. Then doctors can replace it.", "w_transplant": "This word means replacing an unhealthy organ with a healthy one. It has two beats.", "n_transplant": "Transplant.", "s_trans": "Trans.", "s_plant": "Plant.", "trans_means": "Trans means across. The organ goes across, from one person to another.", "donor": "The healthy organ usually comes from a person who has recently died.", "donor_gift": "It's a very kind gift. It can save someone's life.", "sushruta": "Long ago, a doctor in India called Sushruta mended skin, using nearby skin.", "sushruta_when": "That was about two thousand seven hundred years ago!", "today_q": "What can doctors transplant today? Tap all the ones you think.", "sleepy_no": "Snooze! You can't transplant sleepiness!", "today_ans": "All of them! Hearts, lungs, livers and kidneys. Even faces, arms and legs!", "urea": "Your kidneys take a waste called urea out of your blood. It goes into urine.", "kidney_fail": "If kidneys stop working, urea builds up. Too much can harm organs, like the heart.", "dialysis_what": "A machine can clean the blood instead. This is called dialysis.", "dt_sort": "Dialysis or transplant? Sort each card into the right box.", "dt_hours": "Dialysis takes many hours, every week.", "dt_nodonor": "Dialysis doesn't need a donor.", "dt_nomeds": "Dialysis doesn't need medicines for the rest of your life.", "dt_normal": "A transplant lets people live a more normal life. They can even go on holiday!", "dt_meds": "After a transplant, people take medicines for the rest of their life.", "dt_needdonor": "A transplant needs a suitable donor. And sometimes it doesn't work.", "dt_done": "Both treatments help people. Each one has good points and harder points.", "card_intro": "Some people carry an organ donor card. It says they want to help others, after they die.", "card_other": "Some people have a different idea. Carry a card only if you don't want to donate.", "card_talk": "What do you think? There's no right answer. Talk about it with your grown-up.", "hosp_done": "Hospital visit done. You were calm and kind, like a real doctor.", "wrong": "Hmm, think again. You can do it.", "wrong2": "Nearly! Have another look.", "teach_intro": "Yawn… Snooze's sleepiness is catching. My brain is muddled. Can you teach me?", "m1": "An organ system is just one big organ. Is that right?", "m1_fix": "Oh! It's a group of organs, working together. Thank you!", "m2": "The breathing system carries oxygen all around the body. Is that right?", "m2_fix": "I see! Breathing only takes oxygen in. The circulatory system carries it round.", "m3": "The Egyptians were right. The heart's tubes carry air. Is that right?", "m3_fix": "Of course! They carry blood. The air was only there in dead bodies.", "m4": "Plants are just plants. They don't have organ systems. Is that right?", "m4_fix": "Silly me! Plants have a water transport system. Roots, stem and leaves.", "m5": "The ladder goes organ, tissue, cell, then organ system. Is that right?", "m5_fix": "Oops! Cell, tissue, organ, organ system, organism. Can Tiny Owls Sing Opera!", "teach_wrong": "Hmm, are you sure? Let's check our town map together.", "teach_done": "You're a brilliant teacher! I'm wide awake now.", "finish": "Body Town is fixed! The Grand Opening can begin.", "ribbon": "Snooze, will you cut the ribbon? Oh. With your teeth. Okay!", "bigideas1": "Big idea one. Cells make tissues. Tissues make organs. Organs make organ systems.", "bigideas2": "Big idea two. Your body has six systems. Can Dogs Usually Nap By Lakes?", "bigideas3": "Big idea three. Plants have a water transport system: roots, stem and leaves.", "unit_recap": "That's the end of unit 7A! Life processes, organs, tissues, cells and systems. Wow!", "snooze_bye": "Snooze says thank you. He's going for a well-earned nap. By the lake.", "cert": "Here is your certificate. You are a Unit 7A Champion!", "next": "Next time, a new unit: sexual reproduction in animals. Goodbye from Body Town!", "p1": "Well done!", "p2": "Brilliant!", "p3": "You got it!", "p4": "Super thinking!", "p5": "Great job!", "p6": "Fantastic!", "p7": "Yes! Even Snooze is wagging his tail!"};
